            <ArticleTitle>[Amputation stump pain: a therapeutic study (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>245-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study has been done in a Thermal Army Hospital, concerning the suffering of amputed persons and their treatment by &quot;tiapride&quot;. For 20 observations, it has been noted 11 excellent and 6 good results, by a mean treatment of 300 mg. Interesting results are particularly observed at the first appearance of the soreness, a better integration of this one has been proved, it has also been noticed that amputed patients tolerate much better their prosthesis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
